{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the ravine of the streams</b> — ס\"ת (notarikon of the final letters) דם, for the blood would flow down from the slain who were killed in the ravine." "<b>As a settlement</b> — twice in the Masorah: לשבת ער, לשבת אברם, for in the merit of Abraham they merited this. Another interpretation: this is what we say in the Gemara — one who married a woman and stayed with her ten years and she bore no child, he may divorce her, and we learn it from what is written: מקץ עשר שנים לשבת אברם בארץ כנען, for he took Hagar, and that is לשבת ער — one who remains childless may marry another woman, and how much? After ten years." "<b>And it leaned</b> — twice in the Masorah: ונשען לגבול מואב, ונשען על ה׳ קדוש ישראל באמת, for when they came to the border of Moab and saw the miracles performed for them, they leaned on HaShem, the Holy One of Israel, in truth."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:46.307258855Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}